feat(serve): wire the three ingestion tools, and refuse a tool nobody decided (#211)

RM-126, RM-127 and RM-128 each shipped a bound tool that cmd/innsegl never
configured. All three were advertised on tools/list, accepted by the transport
and reported present by MissingTools(), and answered INVARIANT_VIOLATION to
every input. The defect survived two waves and was found sideways: the contract
tests could not drive any of the three through the shipped wiring and had to
install the configuration themselves, which three doc comments said in as many
words and could do nothing about.

Driven by MCP-058 (the start-up refusal and its message), MCP-059 (the three
settings as flags and environment, with serve's validation shape) and MCP-060
(every tool the contract stack binds answers a verdict about its input and
never its own unwired gate). MCP-060 was observed failing first, naming
describe_workspace, observe_tool_call and observe_session.

describe_workspace, observe_tool_call and observe_session are now configured
from -host-projects/$INNSEGL_HOST_PROJECTS, -projects-mount, -observe-body-dir/
$INNSEGL_MCP_LOG_DIR and -session-dir/$INNSEGL_MCP_SESSION_DIR, each opt-in on
sign_commit's terms because none has a defensible default. A relative path for
any of them is refused by name, and a marker volume with no host root is
refused too: observe_session resolves the workspace through describe_workspace
on every start.

The guard against the next one is toolWiring. Every Configure call goes through
install(), which takes that call's own two return values, and every deliberate
non-configuration through withhold(), written where the deployment's opt-in is
read. A tool on a served surface that appears in neither stops the process by
name before a listener opens. The record is a by-product of configuring rather
than a list beside it, which is the defect one layer up.

The contract stack now wires all eight tools, so the MCP-006 battery installs
nothing of its own; the two hostile-volume fixtures stay, because a volume that
cannot be written to is a fixture a cell needs and a missing configuration is
not. The battery's sign_commit mutation guard is generalised to all eight.

deploy/compose/innsegl.workrepo.yml sets the two volumes beside the host root
it already sets: the bodies share innsegl-api's and innsegl-reconciler's
directory read-write, and the session markers get a named volume with no reader
outside the MCP.

